rror_code, match count, byte size, budget value, remedy.'"],"finding":"The regression-coverage AC ties its asserted remedy example to list_tickets, but a separate AC requires ready_tickets' refusal to name next_batch(epic_id) rather than the filter-based remedy list_tickets uses. The coverage AC does not explicitly require asserting that ready_tickets' refusal carries ITS tool-appropriate remedy vocabulary, so a test could pass while ready_tickets emits list_tickets' has_tag remedy (arguments ready_tickets rejects).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcbee55f6cf3f6c83","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC 'Regression coverage asserts the error's CONTENTS' vs AC 'The remedy must be one the REFUSED TOOL can execute'","norm_id":"nc81274929d3ecd2e","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["ready_tickets refuses but emits the list_tickets has_tag remedy; the caller is told to use a filter ready_tickets does not accept, and the suite stays green because no test asserts the tool-specific remedy string"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify WHERE match count / byte size / budget live in the refusal (structured fields vs a defined substring format inside `message`), since error_envelope carries only {error, input, message, exit_code?}.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Carries error_code=\"response_too_large\", naming match count, byte size, budget and a remedy.'","Plan: 'Regression coverage asserts the error's CONTENTS ... error_code, match count, byte size, budget value, remedy.'","error_envelope(error, input_str, message, exit_code) builds env = {\"error\":..., \"input\":..., \"message\":...} with only an optional exit_code — no count/bytes/budget field (src/rebar/_engine_support/output.py:141)","Plan: 'no schema change (error_envelope.error is an open string, not an enum)' — so no new structured field is being added"],"finding":"The structured refusal must 'carry' error_code, match count, byte size, budget and a remedy, and regression tests must assert each as a distinct value — but the emitted error_envelope shape is only {error, input, message, exit_code?} (src/rebar/_engine_support/output.py:134), which has no structured slot for match count / byte size / budget. The plan never states these are packed into the free-text `message` (and in what format) versus carried as structured fields, so the LLM-consumed contract's value locations are undefined.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f49dfc99fda868ebd","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC lines: 'Structured refusal, right exception TYPE, closed vocabulary' and 'Regression coverage asserts the error's CONTENTS'","norm_id":"n5fe23f68948e5382","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An agent parsing the refusal to programmatically decide how much to narrow needs the budget/actual bytes as machine-readable values, but they arrive only as prose inside `message`","The regression test asserting 'byte size' and 'budget value' has no defined field/format to match against"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the remedy prose in `message` embeds match count, byte size, and budget in a fixed, test-assertable format (e.g. 'N tickets, X bytes exceed the 90000-byte budget'), and have the regression tests assert those exact substrings — or add explicit structured fields and update the schema accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the rollback path (revert + redeploy) and whether the byte bound/refusal reaches production via a flag or is a single 100%-traffic flip, given ready_tickets' ~1.7% headroom makes refusal a near-term production state.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Both list tools bound at the same 90,000-byte _WORKFLOW_TOKEN_BUDGET_BYTES'","'Its measured headroom is ~1.7% (see comment), so refusing is a near-term state'","'the container must have redeployed and served the call' — single deployed endpoint, no canary/flag mentioned"],"finding":"The plan makes a hard behavior change to the deployed MCP server for all traffic at once: both list tools narrow their default output and ready_tickets can now REFUSE with response_too_large (measured headroom ~1.7%, so refusal is a near-term state). There is no staged rollout/canary and no stated rollback path beyond the implicit git-revert; the refusal itself has no per-call opt-out (full=True restores bytes but does not raise the byte budget), so a legitimately-sized ready_tickets response that crosses 90,000 bytes gets refused for every caller the moment the container redeploys.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffe75d3d3af6135ea","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC 'Bounded, measured at a named seam' and 'The remedy must be one the REFUSED TOOL can execute'","norm_id":"nb374972c3cbf1551","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["ready_tickets crosses the 90K bound in production after redeploy and every client is refused with no way to raise the budget; the only recovery is a code revert + redeploy","A caller that relied on the fuller default list payload gets the narrowed projection with no gradual rollout window to detect breakage"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a note naming the revert-and-redeploy rollback, and consider gating the new refusal behind an env/config-adjustable budget (or an initial log-only warn phase) so a bound crossing does not hard-refuse all ready_tickets traffic on first deploy.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Enumerate list_states' non-artifact consumers (reads_cli.py CLI `list`, validate._raw_tickets, next_batch) and state whether each retains prior fields or is intentionally narrowed by the shared lean_projection.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC-2: 'called by BOTH backends: `list_states` and `_snapshot/ticket_view.py::TicketView.list_by_query`'","src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py:344: `results = list_states(tracker, TicketQuery(**opts))` (CLI `list` arm)","src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py:67: `return reads.list_states(tracker)` (validate._raw_tickets)","src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py:144: `_reads.list_states(tracker, TicketQuery(status=\"open,in_progress\"))`"],"finding":"The plan names list_states as the backend where the shared lean_projection is applied, but does not enumerate list_states' consumers outside the artifact directory (_engine_support/reads.py) whose default output could be affected by dropping signature fields at the list_states seam.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb918f8796325d0bb","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, bullet 'One shared lean projection' (AC-2)","norm_id":"n2f7811db4d13f03d","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If lean_projection lands inside list_states, the CLI list / validate / next_batch paths that call list_states must be confirmed to retain their prior field shape (signature material) or be intentionally narrowed."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how error_code='response_too_large' is attached to the raised RebarError (dedicated subclass, constructor kwarg, or explicit attribute set), since RebarError does not set .error_code and step-5 classification depends on it.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7413,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Raises a rebar._errors.RebarError ... Carries error_code=\"response_too_large\"' and 'error_code_for needs no change (step 5 returns a non-empty exc.error_code)'","RebarError.__init__(self, message, *, returncode=1, stderr=\"\") sets only returncode and stderr; no error_code attribute (src/rebar/_errors.py:22-25)","error_code_for step 5: code = getattr(exc, \"error_code\", None); if code: return code (src/rebar/_errors.py:132-135)"],"finding":"The plan requires raising rebar._errors.RebarError 'carrying error_code=\"response_too_large\"' and relies on error_code_for step 5 (a non-empty exc.error_code) to classify it — but RebarError.__init__ takes only (message, returncode, stderr) and never sets .error_code (src/rebar/_errors.py:19-25). The plan does not specify the mechanism to attach error_code to the raised instance (a new subclass, a constructor change, or post-construction attribute assignment), which is the load-bearing hook for the entire structured-error path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd5fef0fac0e3218","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC line: 'Structured refusal, right exception TYPE, closed vocabulary'","norm_id":"n82187438d5050780","priority":0.0587,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor instantiates RebarError('...') without setting .error_code; step 5 finds no attribute, falls through to step 7 'command_failed', and the closed-vocabulary 'response_too_large' code is never emitted"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Define a small RebarError subclass (or set exc.error_code = 'response_too_large' on the instance before raising) so error_code_for step 5 returns it deterministically.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","seve